<title>POLAND: BYTOM FALLS 9.9 PCT AFTER LAY-OFF NEWS.</title>
<headline>BYTOM FALLS 9.9 PCT AFTER LAY-OFF NEWS.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Polish garment maker Bytom SA fell 9.9 percent to 28.3 zlotys the session after it announced it was laying off 288 workers to cut production, traders said.</p>
<p>Garment maker Vistula , which fell 5.9 percent to 9.6 zlotys, has said it was considering dismissing 206 workers to shift production from unprofitable exports.</p>
<p>&quot;It could be a bad sign for the firms that they haven't gained large enough markets,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Post-price-fixing selling for Bytom was strong enough for investors to have their bids reduced.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
